]

# --- Wine Mono + Gecko (Adobe prefixes need them INSTALLED, never suppressed) ----
# The Wine Mono/Gecko installer popup must never reach the end user, but the WRONG
# way to dodge it is WINEDLLOVERRIDES="mscoree,mshtml=..." on the LAUNCH path — that
# leaves gecko uninstalled and CLOBBERS Adobe's mshtml-backed web content (sign-in).
# The RIGHT way (a complete Adobe prefix, e.g. the proven mudhut-accc2, has both Mono
# and Gecko installed): actually INSTALL the matching versions during provision so
# wineboot never prompts at launch and nothing is disabled. The versions MUST match
# what the packaged neutron-wine runtime expects (baked at build time: appwiz.cpl
# MONO_VERSION / mshtml GECKO_VERSION) — a version skew is exactly what makes wineboot
# re-prompt on a prefix-update. Keep these in lockstep with build/WINE_BASE.
